<article class="env-corollary" id="31C7FC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/31C7FC">Corollary <span data-tag="31C7FC">3.2.2.13</span>.</a> Let $p: X \rightarrow S$ be a Cartesian fibration of simplicial sets, and let $q: Y \rightarrow S$ be a coCartesian fibration. Define a new simplicial set $T$ equipped with a map $T \rightarrow S$ by the formula </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Hom _{S}(K, T) \simeq \Hom _{S}( X \times _{S} K, Y). \]
</div>
  <p> Then: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The projection $r: T \rightarrow S$ is a coCartesian fibration. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
An edge $\Delta ^1 \rightarrow Z$ is $r$-coCartesian if and only if the induced map $\Delta ^1 \times _{S} X \rightarrow \Delta ^1 \times _{S} Y$ carries $p$-Cartesian edges to $q$-coCartesian edges. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Corollary <a href="/tag/9E689D" data-tag="9E689D">3.2.2.12</a> in the case where $Z = S$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>